<title>USA: EA Industries Q1 net loss narrows.</title>
<headline>EA Industries Q1 net loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>WEST LONG BRANCH, N.J. 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended</p>
<p>					  (Thousands except share data)</p>
<p>					Mar 29,		     Mar 30,</p>
<p>					  1997			1996(1)</p>
<p> Net Sales			  $14,625		     $24,025</p>
<p> Cost of Sales		     14,460			22,634</p>
<p> SG&amp;A				   1,901			 2,220</p>
<p> Loss from Operations	   (1,736)			 (829)</p>
<p> Net Loss			   (2,603)		     (3,869)</p>
<p> Loss per Common Share	   (0.35)			(0.93)</p>
<p>Weighted Average Common</p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding	  7,442,863		   4,154,236</p>
<p>NOTE: (1) Results have been reclassified to conform to 1997 presentation; including adjustment to give retroactive effect to a one-for-four reverse split effective as of the close of business on December 27, 1996 and adjustment to reflect the amortization of incremental yield included in conversion terms of debentures issued in 1995 and 1996.</p>
<p>Q1 1996 net loss includes $2.2 million charge for amortization of fixed discount feature of convertible notes.</p>
<p>EA Industries Inc.</p>
